caption: Design Summary
technology-rule: design-summary

Choose the intended species or substrate, standard dose and scaling, and applicable design and manufacturing skills.

Choose the positive effects.

Assign one allowed origin modifier to every supernatural advantage.

Give every integrated effect the same onset, duration, and common modifiers.

Calculate Level Load.

Calculate Design Point Load.

Calculate Benefit Value without harmful side-effect discounts.

Determine Required Talent.

Calculate Effective Talent from actual Talent and TL.

Allocate excess Talent as Refinement.

Calculate the addiction roll.

Make the Concept roll normally; it determines whether the theory works but does not affect cost.

Determine complexity, calculate Effective Prototype Skill, and make the Prototype roll.

Calculate Normal Market Cost and Production Cost from DPL, Cost Refinement, and margin of success.

Record the intended species or substrate, standard dose and scaling, clearance time, Redosing behavior, counteragents or special formula interactions, and overdose behavior.
